{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"symmetry reduction in thermal geometry symmetry reduction in thermal geometry","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry.md","fileName":"Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Finite Element Thermal Modeling]] [[Simulation Geometry Quality]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Finite Element Thermal Modeling","Simulation Geometry Quality","Thermal Mesh Refinement","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"symmetry reduction in thermal geometry symmetry reduction in thermal geometry","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry.md","fileName":"Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry","heading":"Symmetry Reduction in Thermal Geometry","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Geometric symmetry can reduce a model to a fraction of the physical object when temperature and heat flux repeat across the omitted sectors. A symmetry boundary prevents normal heat flow across the cut plane and represents the mirrored continuation of the domain.\n\nThe reduction is invalid if an asymmetric source, material, flow, or boundary condition breaks the repeated pattern. When applicable, it permits finer [[Thermal Mesh Refinem